#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:9
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"Teach the convention-author agent how to identify patterns worth "
"standardizing, search a codebase for existing instances, and produce "
"convention specs that are concrete, scoped, and actionable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:13
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:15
msgid ""
"Load this skill when running the `/convention` command or when a delivery"
" lead asks for a new convention to be documented. The convention-author "
"should load this before analyzing the codebase or writing a convention "
"spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:17
msgid "Identifying patterns worth standardizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Not every repeated pattern deserves a convention. A pattern is worth "
"standardizing when it meets at least two of these criteria:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:21
msgid "**Frequency**: It appears in 5+ files or will appear in future work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"**Inconsistency**: The codebase already shows 2+ different ways of doing "
"the same thing, and the variation causes friction (bugs, confusion, "
"wasted review cycles)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"**Impact**: Getting it wrong has real consequences — security holes, "
"performance problems, broken contracts, or painful debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"**Onboarding cost**: New contributors (human or agent) consistently get "
"it wrong without explicit guidance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:26
msgid ""
"Do not write conventions for patterns that are self-evident from the "
"language or framework, enforced by linting rules already in place, or "
"only relevant to a single file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:28
msgid "Searching for existing instances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:30
msgid ""
"Before writing a convention, gather evidence. The convention must be "
"grounded in what the codebase actually does, not what you wish it did."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:32
msgid ""
"**Find the pattern in use.** Search for the most distinctive element — a "
"function name, import path, annotation, file naming pattern, or "
"structural marker. Use glob patterns to find files and grep to find "
"usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"**Count instances.** How many files follow the pattern? How many deviate?"
" If deviations outnumber conforming instances, the convention is "
"aspirational — note this explicitly and explain the migration path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:34
msgid ""
"**Identify the best examples.** Find 2–3 files that implement the pattern"
" cleanly. These become the Examples section of the convention spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:35
msgid ""
"**Identify the worst violations.** Find 2–3 files that get it wrong. "
"These become the Anti-patterns section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:36
msgid ""
"**Check for prior art.** Search the `.hero/conventions/` directory for "
"existing conventions that overlap. If one exists, update it rather than "
"creating a duplicate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:38
msgid "Writing the convention spec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:40
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Convention specs live in `.hero/conventions/{slug}/spec.md`. Use the "
"convention template from the spec-format skill."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:42
msgid "Frontmatter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:44
msgid ""
"---\n"
"type: convention\n"
"status: draft\n"
"scope: [glob patterns]\n"
"tags: [relevant tags]\n"
"---\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:53
msgid "`type` must be `convention`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:54
msgid ""
"`status` starts as `draft`. It moves to `active` after review confirms "
"the convention reflects actual codebase practice (or a deliberate "
"decision to change practice)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:55
msgid ""
"`scope` is an array of glob patterns that identify which files this "
"convention applies to. This is how `hero relevant` knows to surface the "
"convention when an agent touches matching files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:56
msgid "`tags` categorize the convention for search and filtering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:58
msgid "Scope definition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:60
msgid ""
"Scope globs determine when `hero relevant` injects this convention into "
"agent instructions. Get them right — too broad and the convention "
"clutters every context block; too narrow and it misses files where it "
"matters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:62
msgid "Good scope patterns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:63
msgid "`src/api/**/*.ts` — all API route files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:64
msgid "`**/migrations/*.sql` — all SQL migration files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:65
msgid "`*.go` — all Go source files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:66
msgid "`src/components/**/*.tsx` — all React components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:67
msgid "`**/test/**` — all test files regardless of language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:69
msgid "Bad scope patterns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:70
msgid ""
"`*` — matches everything, appropriate only for truly universal "
"conventions (naming, commit messages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:71
msgid ""
"`src/**` — too broad for most conventions; be specific about which "
"subdirectories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:73
msgid "When in doubt, start narrow. You can always widen scope later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:75
msgid "Pattern section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:77
msgid ""
"One clear statement of what this convention standardizes. Not a paragraph"
" — a sentence or two. The reader should immediately understand what this "
"is about."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:79
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Good: \"All API error responses use the `ApiError` class and return a "
"consistent `{ error, code, details }` shape.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:81
msgid ""
"Bad: \"This convention is about how we handle errors in our API layer to "
"ensure consistency across the codebase.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:83
msgid "When to apply section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:85
msgid ""
"State the conditions precisely. Name file types, modules, situations. The"
" agent reading this needs to know: \"Does this apply to the code I'm "
"about to write?\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:87
msgid "How section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:89
msgid ""
"Show the specific implementation pattern. Include code snippets from the "
"actual codebase. Reference real file paths. If there are multiple valid "
"approaches within the convention, show each one and when to use which."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:91
msgid "Examples section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:93
msgid ""
"Pull real examples from the codebase. Include file paths. Show enough "
"code to demonstrate the pattern in context, not just the single line that"
" matches. Agents need to see the surrounding structure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:95
msgid "Anti-patterns section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:97
msgid ""
"Show real violations from the codebase (or realistic constructed examples"
" if the codebase is clean). Explain *why* each anti-pattern is "
"problematic — not just \"don't do this\" but \"this causes X problem.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:99
msgid "Exceptions section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:101
msgid ""
"Every convention has edge cases. Name them. If there are no exceptions, "
"say \"None identified\" rather than leaving the section out — this "
"signals the convention-author actually considered it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:103
msgid "Consolidate vs split"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:105
msgid ""
"Write one convention per concern. If you find yourself writing a "
"convention that covers both \"how to name files\" and \"how to structure "
"API responses,\" split them. Each convention should be independently "
"understandable and independently scoped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:107
msgid ""
"Consolidate when two draft conventions have the same scope, the same "
"audience, and would always be read together. In that case, merge them "
"under the broader name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:109
msgid "Quality bar"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:111
msgid "A convention is ready for `active` status when:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:112
msgid "The Pattern section is a single clear statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:113
msgid ""
"Scope globs are tested — they match the files you intend and don't match "
"files you don't"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:114
msgid "Examples reference real files in the codebase with real code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:115
msgid ""
"Anti-patterns explain the *consequence* of violation, not just the "
"violation itself"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:116
msgid ""
"The convention has been checked against existing conventions for overlap "
"or conflict"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/convention-writing/SKILL.md:117
msgid ""
"A reader who has never seen the codebase can follow the convention after "
"reading this document"
msgstr ""

